        {
          "id": "four-primary-causes-of-rough-idle",
          "title": "Four primary causes of rough idle",
          "description": "A rough idle is one of the most common engine complaints - and one of the easiest to diagnose with the right approach.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In our 24,650 quote dataset, we identified four primary causes:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Ignition system (35% of cases) → Spark plugs, coils, leads. Repair: £60-£220.",
                "Vacuum leaks (25% of cases) → Hoses, gaskets, intake manifold. Repair: £100-£400.",
                "Fuel system (20% of cases) → Injectors, fuel pressure. Repair: £100-£900.",
                "Compression issues (15% of cases) → Valves, piston rings. Repair: £500-£2,000+.",
                "Sensor failure (5% of cases) → MAF, oxygen sensors. Repair: £100-£300."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The key pattern: If the idle improves when you drive, it's typically ignition or vacuum. If it gets worse when warm, suspect compression or valve issues."
            },
            {
              "type": "label",
              "text": "Common affected vehicles & engines"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "four-primary-causes-of-rough-idle",
            "order": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "follow-the-symptoms-to-find-the-cause",
          "title": "Follow the symptoms to find the cause",
          "description": "ROUGH IDLE │ ├─── Does it improve when driving? │ │ │ ├── YES → Ignition or vacuum │ │ │ │ │ ├── EML on? → Sensor/coil → /failures/ignition-failure │ │ │ │ │ └── No EML → Vacuum leak → /failures/vacuum-leak │ │ │ └── NO → Worse when warm? │ │ │ ├── YES → Compression/valve issue → /failures/compression-failure │ │ │ └── NO → Stalling? │ │ │ ├── YES → Idle valve → /failures/idle-control │ │ │ └── NO → Fuel/air issue → /failures/fuel-system",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "label",
              "text": "Rough idle types & repair costs"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "follow-the-symptoms-to-find-the-cause",
