          }
        },
        {
          "id": "when-rough-idle-needs-urgent-attention",
          "title": "⚠️ WHEN ROUGH IDLE NEEDS URGENT ATTENTION",
          "description": "Rough idle is rarely an emergency - but these symptoms require prompt action:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Flashing engine light → Active misfire - STOP DRIVING",
                "Rough idle + loss of power → Multiple causes",
                "Rough idle + stalling → Safety issue",
                "Rough idle + overheating → Head gasket risk"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The Flashing Light Danger: If your check engine light is flashing, unburnt fuel is entering the exhaust system and destroying your catalytic converter (£500-£2,500 repair)."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Book Diagnostic"
            },
            {
              "type": "cards",
              "cards": [
                {
                  "title": "What happens if you ignore it",
                  "text": "The Hidden Cost: Ignoring rough idle can damage your catalytic converter - £500-£2,500 to replace.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "What happens if you ignore it The hidden cost of ignoring rough idle Symptom Progression Cost Impact Rough idle (ignition) Misfire, cat damage £60-£220 → £2,000+ Rough idle (vacuum) Lean condition, engine damage £100-£400 → £2,500+ Rough idle (injector) Cylinder wash, bore damage £100-£900 → £2,500-£10,000+ The Hidden Cost: Ignoring rough idle can damage your catalytic converter - £500-£2,500 to replace."
                },
                {
                  "title": "What to do next",
                  "text": "Step 1: Check Engine Light - Is the EML on? Is it flashing? (STOP DRIVING if flashing) Step 2: Note The Pattern - Does it improve when driving? Is it worse when warm? Does it stall? Step 3: Professional Diagnostic (£50-£150) - A technician will read fault codes, check live data (fuel trims, MAF), test ignition system, check for vacuum leaks, and perform compression test if required.",
                  "highlight": "",
